  <event id="83">
      <start>16:30</start>
      <duration>00:45</duration>
      <room>H.2214</room>
      <slug></slug>
      <title>Drupal and the semantic web</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>Drupal</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;As of Drupal 7 will use RDFa markup in core, in this session I will:&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt; explain what the implications are of this and why this matters&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt; give a short introduction to the Semantic web, RDF, RDFa and SPARQL in human language&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt; give a short overview of the RDF modules that are available in contrib&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt; talk about some of the potential use cases of all these magical technologies&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;  </abstract>
      <description></description>
      <persons>
          <person id="831">Kristof van Tomme</person>
      </persons>
      <links></links>
      <video></video>
      <end></end>
  </event>